Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginEnable = Enable Google login
Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginEnableHelp = Enables Dolibarr's native Google OAuth provider as a primary login method delegated through Krea2FactorAuth. Google-authenticated logins skip the local TOTP challenge after domain and lock-policy checks pass.
Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginAllowedDomains = Allowed Google email domains
Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginAllowedDomainsHelp = Optional comma-separated domain allow-list for Google login. Leave empty to allow any Google account that Dolibarr maps to an existing user email or OAuth email.
Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginUseExtrafieldEmail = Use user-card Google login email
Krea2FactorAuthGoogleLoginUseExtrafieldEmailHelp = When enabled, Google OAuth login must match the user's Krea2FactorAuth email extrafield. The standard Dolibarr user email and OAuth email are no longer accepted for Google login unless they match that extrafield. When disabled, the extrafield is hidden on the user card.
