Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyTitle = Privacy Policy
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyIntro = This privacy policy explains how the Google login integration provided by Krea2FactorAuth handles information when it is installed on a Dolibarr ERP/CRM instance.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyDataTitle = Information processed
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyDataIdentity = Google identity information requested through OpenID Connect scopes: account identifier, email address, and basic profile information.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyDataAccount = Dolibarr user account information needed to match the Google identity to an existing authorized user.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyDataSession = Technical login session data needed by Dolibarr and Krea2FactorAuth to complete authentication and apply configured access-policy checks.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyUseTitle = How information is used
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyUseText = Information obtained during Google login is used to authenticate the user, match the Google account to a Dolibarr user, and apply configured access-policy checks. It is not used for advertising or profiling.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacySharingTitle = Sharing
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacySharingText = Krea2FactorAuth does not sell Google identity data. Google login data is processed inside the Dolibarr installation operated by the organization using this module, subject to that organization's internal access and retention rules.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyStorageTitle = Storage
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyStorageText = The module does not store Google passwords. OAuth client credentials are stored only by Dolibarr administrators using Dolibarr configuration constants. User two-factor secrets are stored separately from Google identity data.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacySecurityTitle = Security
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacySecurityText = Production Google OAuth login should use HTTPS and an authorized redirect URI that matches the Dolibarr callback URL configured in Google Auth Platform.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyContactTitle = Contact
Krea2FactorAuthPublicPrivacyContactText = For privacy questions, contact the organization operating this Dolibarr instance or the support email configured on the Google OAuth consent screen.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsTitle = Terms of Service
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsIntro = These terms describe the use of Google login for a Dolibarr ERP/CRM installation protected by Krea2FactorAuth.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsAccessTitle = Authorized access
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsAccessText = Google login is intended only for users authorized by the organization operating this Dolibarr instance. A successful Google authentication does not grant access unless Dolibarr maps the Google account to an existing permitted user.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsSecurityTitle = Account security
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsSecurityText = Users are responsible for keeping their Google account secure and complying with the local access and security requirements configured by the operator.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsOperatorTitle = Operator responsibility
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsOperatorText = The organization operating the Dolibarr instance is responsible for user access rights, business data, retention rules, compliance obligations, and support for its users.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsGoogleTitle = Google services
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsGoogleText = Google authentication is provided by Google. Use of a Google account remains subject to Google's applicable terms and policies.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsLicenseTitle = Module license
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsLicenseText = These terms do not modify the GPL-3.0-or-later license that applies to the Krea2FactorAuth module source code.
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsContactTitle = Contact
Krea2FactorAuthPublicTermsContactText = For service questions, contact the organization operating this Dolibarr instance or the support email configured on the Google OAuth consent screen.
